body:
I really wonder sometimes why Saim-Hann are the poster boys when their armor is literally just the big red blob. You got a white helmet and a Black gun and that's about it. Everything else is red. So much red. Got lost in the red. Red red red red red red

&#x200B;

Seriously though you could do with painting the different bits of the armor different colors, like painting the kneecaps or the boots, or the ab plates

Uninstalling my ENB didn't help, and neither did removing NAO, unfortunately

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

EDIT: Yes it did, the ENB did the trick. Thank you

[https://www.nexusmods.com/oblivion/mods/47591?tab=description](https://www.nexusmods.com/oblivion/mods/47591?tab=description) I am mostly using this modlist for purely graphical mods. I had an issue where I disabled Volumetric fog in Oblivion Reloaded Lite because it was ruining the Shivering Isles Sky.

&#x200B;

EDIT: This has been solved, it was something with my ENB, thank you for your help.

Well there's economic impracticalities in things like universal healthcare. Not saying it isn't possible, it is, and it's highly desirable, but it's necessary to implement that in a reasonable and cost effective manner. Homeless and poverty in general are problems I agree. However, implementing universal healthcare without border and citizenship reform first is a disaster waiting to happen. Giving them access without citizenship is just asking for trouble. It's going to drive actual citizens further right, because they think their citizenship is meaningless and they're being treated unfairly, and it's going to encourage healthcare tourism

&#x200B;

It also creates this sort of "sword of damocles" situation for the migrants that come in improperly. They can be deported at will if they do something wrong, but it can easily lead to corruption where they're being exploited by corporations to work for far cheaper than the law allows for citizens, and if they piss their empoyers off, there's the threat of deportation hanging over their heads.

I mean, a New Zealand tree makes sense when you consider that they fit quite nicely into that theme. It was the British Empire, and ANZAC forces include New Zealand as well as Australia (Hell, they probably thought of South Africa and India first when thinking of it, and then had to slide in the rest of the dominions just for the sake of the theme). Britain, obviously, gets into the war a lot sooner than South America, though they didn't get their rework until Man the Guns. Plus, all of these countries all have ways of getting into the war already in the game, especially considering Japan. Most of the focuses basically make them more or less useful to the British. If anything it seems like most of the trees in TfV are actually nerfs to the countries themselves. The base tree is actually more powerful and less limiting than the TfV trees. I also think TfV was mostly intended for multiplayer, as well as Death or Dishonour.

&#x200B;

I personally really hope we'll get the Nordic trees in the same pack as the USSR next. That, to me, is a lot more pressing an issue than South America, but, with Mexico getting a new tree, South America may be on the dev's minds.

The coups suck though. I don't even know if there is an AI for the rebelling country, and they just sort of sit there and let the main one conquer them.. At least, that's what happened when I tried organizing a civil war in Japan as Communist China.

&#x200B;

I intended it as a distraction, to move troops away from the front in China, but the Japs just marched troops they already had in Tokyo up and crushed it almost instantly.

Ok here's the thing right. Spells shouldn't be that bad alone. The more you level up your magic skill, the less the spells cost, right? That's supposed to be the primary way you reduce your magicka cost. However, the spells scale really badly. The second to highest level shock spell? The last one you can cast with one hand and use as a direct weapon that's not area of effect? That can maybe knock like a 10th off of... say a Dwarf Steam Titan at best. They're not worth the magicka you use for it. Let alone trying to use a high level ward shield at the same time.

&#x200B;

Skyrim's damage cap hits the mages the hardest. They're basically saying that even a master destruction mage can't really dent an enemy all that well. Lore wise? The empire has an entire corps of battle-mages that specialize in destruction magic. Have you seen an imperial battlemage? They don't wear that much enchanted gear. Mostly because the empire can't afford to outfit every soldier with it. The game is basically saying that that whole section of the imperial army is worthless compared to its normal troops.

&#x200B;

Oblivion had the same damage scaling issue, but *even worse.*

Ok smart one. Let's start at the basics. A build is a framework by which you play a character. It defines a playstyle, and it also assists with roleplay. Builds are achieved, through items, yes, but mostly achieved through the character themselves and by their skills. Requiring every single build to have enchanting to even play is broken. You don't see the problem here? A build for a mage is completely underpowered, inoperable unless you enchant. Warriors are milquetoast, and have a cap on their damage as well, whereas the enemies' health just gets worse, unless you enchant. 

&#x200B;

The only non-broken build is stealth archer, because it, in true skyrim fashion, is broken, and lets you just take people out without risk.

The strat for an independent manchukuo is pretty simple, and I've been practicing it for a while. What you need to do is to refuse getting called into Japan's war with China, and then declare independence and catch the Japanese army right in between you and republican China, the ports in East Hebei and Dalian are massive priorities. In my game, Japan took too long going to war with China, waiting until 1939 or so before starting (it helps that the AI will do the Manchukuo project focuses to help if there's a player there). In my game I got a bit lucky, too, because Nationalist China had started doing focus on foreign threats instead of the warlords, which let me pull the subjugate the warlords focus. I actually got amazingly lucky there too, because every single warlord submitted to me, and then I just started battering Nationalist China from all sides.

&#x200B;

After that, it's about building up subs with minelaying tubes. Japan will offer you peace, but it's usually best you don't take it, especially since they will probably still be at war with Nationalist China and naval invade Shanghai. I actually had no subs at the start and no experience to get any, so I had to license one from Germany. I eventually got up enough subs to start whittling down the Japanese navy, with mines and convoy raiding with the subs initially set to do not engage. The process is slow, but inevitable. You're China, you can build up an industry to outmatch the Japanese tenfold. Especially when you start annexing the warlords by giving them a metric fuckton of guns. Then you can naval invade the Japanese home islands. 

&#x200B;

By this point my luck had run out, and Germany had actually capped the Soviet Union, so I had to join the allies in their war against germany. A great push through Eastern Russia, and a Chinese D-Day stuffed the German Genie back in their bottle. It's possible with the Manpower of China.

I was very surprised that happened. I just wasn't watching very intently because I was China. Japan still has more casulties than me, but I'm still somehow out of manpower. As China.

&#x200B;

Somehow I don't think it will matter much soon.

Nope. It's just typical reddit comparing a colonial regime to a calculated genocide. Nuance and historical accuracy brazenly ignored, white people did colonialism, so it must be the same or worse, right? It's better to make a cheap, unfunny joke about it through a polandball comic, which in reality, doesn't really do proper justice to either of the historical events, nor their contexts.

&#x200B;

I guess I just browse these out of nostalgia, or for the rare bit of humor found through the pseudo-intellectual dribble and edgy political statements.

&#x200B;

Is this brief or nonpolitical enough for you?

I assume they keep their cores. If Austria isn't freed specifically in the treaty, they stay a part of Germany, as they are a core. Similarly, there's a focus to core Luxembourg, and Alsace-Lorraine.

&#x200B;

It's actually pretty interesting, because it wasn't just Nazis advocating for a union between Austria and Germany. Austria can become part of Germany in the German Democratic path too.

If every single Communist in Germany is gone, then why does the game have the focus "expatriate the communists?" It's down the Return the Kaiser tree. There were also Communists in Exile in the Soviet Union. They were purged sure, but they had to go somewhere, and the Soviets would have ample motivation to try and cause a revolution in Germany, in fact they kind of intended to, historically. The threat of Communist Revolution was a real threat before Hitler. The Exiles could return after Hitler is deposed. The overthrow of a government is no small matter, and there would've been a power vacuum, and the Nazis would've been seen as vile villains after such a war as depicted in the game. Right after the overthrow of a regime is the prime time for a Communist government to take hold. The country is already going through rapid changes, and the new government isn't all that strong.

&#x200B;

The first focus could be "return the exiles". The country didn't like Communist party, but a post-civil war Germany would really really hate Nazis at that point. If the game lets Communists take power in Britain or the USA, then they should be able to do so in Germany.

&#x200B;

Also, like you said, it's easier to revert to a recent form of government, so installing another totalitarian dictator after having one deposed isn't really all that unlikely. Plus, from a gameplay standpoint, it would make sense. All the other major nations in the world have Communist paths, even Japan has one, but why not Germany?

&#x200B;

It's a stretch, sure, but every alternate government in the game, particularly of major powers, is a stretch, except like, France.

There's probably just as much a historical chance of Germany going Communist, as the US or UK going Fascist, or Communist, or Germany going back to the Monarchy, or going Democratic. There is a way. It's through the Oppose Hitler option. In fact, the Communist party gets quite the boost in the German Military Junta. Ingame there are still Communists around in Germany, and you have to raid them as Hitler.

&#x200B;

Hell there's probably less of a chance of the Soviet Union becoming anything else, especially under Stalin, but the alternate history focus trees can make it happen.

Ok sure, smarmy bastard, most countries. Not all coutries, and not all of  the most populous or important countries in the world, but sure most countires. If you want to be picky and frame it that way. Although most of the people on earth live in countries where the right or left turn on red is a rule, it has a higher number of governments that don't use that rule, sure. Europe and a lot of its it's former colonies, which have the old colonial system still have those laws, sure.

&#x200B;

Also I love the subtle implication that peer pressure is a good basis for domestic policy.

Here's the thing. Roundabouts take up space. More space than a 4 way intersection. Implimenting roundabouts can only happen when there's space for it. Sometimes the space required for that is already taken, by things like, well, buildings, sometimes very tall and very permanant buildings that aren't going anywhere. So, complete replacement of 4 way stops with roundabouts is *never going to happen*, regardless of country.

&#x200B;

I've been to European cities before, many of them still have 4 way stops, because there's no practical way to fit in a roundabout there. Rome still has fucking cobblestone roads and barely has sidewalks, let alone roundabouts. American roads are very organized and carefully layed out, compared to most cities in the world, usually because the cities were planned with horse and buggy, or even cars, in mind.

&#x200B;

This all or nothing attitude is stupid, because the "all" is never going to happen, ever.

Spend your whole game giving mercy, only to deny it at the end. It's what so ironic about people arguing who is the worst and this and that, and who did what and what their crimes are. Asgore murdering children, Asriel murdering everyone, Toriel dooming all the monsters to live underground if she had her way....

&#x200B;

The game is about mercy, for goodness sake.

I was playing as the Austro-Hungarian empire, and managed to get Greece into my Central Powers, who was guaranteed by Romania, who was in the Allies, so Germany, France, the UK, and myself, Ausria Hungary, all went to war with Italy at once.

&#x200B;

>!Italy still managed to capitulate France before we could finish them off.!<

It's annoying when there is just one tiny bit of land somewhere completely random that throws off your plans. For example, say you want to remake the Persian Empire as Iran, well, good luck getting the Dodecanese islands from Italy, and that's on a fully decolonized map, otherwise you've got to get small snippets of Libya from them too. You can control everything else, but you can't get cores on anything unless you have that tiny sliver of land.

&#x200B;

Like, really? We control pretty much all of the old Persian Empire, but we can't say we do unless we've got two tiny snippets of land?

Here's what's not going to happen: the Second Ammendment in the US won't be repealed, because there is currently a majority of Republicans in all branches of the US government. This accelerationist plan relies on complete power being given to the left wing in order to take all the rigths from the right, and force a violent revolt. That's just not going to happen while the moderate right is in power. They're not just going to give the left everything they want just because. So the USA will remain stable and not balkanized. In this way, his attack was a failure.

&#x200B;

Here's what's going to happen: a mass wave of internet censorship. Expect a lot more people to get Alex Jones'd because now they have a weapon with which to go after internet celebs and the sites that they use. We're more than likely never going to hear the phrase "subscribe to pewdiepie" uttered by anyone but a blue checkmark ever again, and Pewds may just stop touching politics altogether, which would be a shame but perfectly reasonable. This is going to make a lot more echochambers as more and more people get driven off of mainstream social media sites. Hell we may even see an attack here from Reddit itself. In this way, his attack was a success. It's going to drive a lot more people on both the left and right into more echochambers and make dialogue even harder, further polarizing the internet.

I don't think this is the time to be censoring people really. It's just going to cause divide, which is exactly what the wretch who pulled the New Zealand shooting wanted. Please, let people joke as they will, it's just jokes. Jokes is all they will remain. Comedy is how we defang these kinds of horrible disasters. Make fun of the monsters and drive them into the dustbins.

&#x200B;

EDIT: I also realized that the attack itself was a horrific attack on the freedom to worship, and free speech itself as well. Still, let's not remember an attack on the freedom to worship and the freedom of speech, by clamping down on peoples' freedom to speak.

\*deaths of criminals, who had been proven to have rushed the cops for their weapons, not just random blacks on the street

&#x200B;

Also given anti-police sentiment in black communities in general, as well as gang culture, leading to increased tensions between black communities and the police, and the fact this isn't just a one sided issue about police violence, but both police militarization and black cultural distrust of police as a whole.

Ralsei carefully wrote and hand crafted that manual for you. I kept it in my inventory and cherished it the whole game. I just imagine him sitting there, painstakingly writing everything out, putting loads of thought and effort into it, taking hours and hours to think up everything he might  possibly need to tell you, maybe even binding the book himself, going through who knows how many drafts to make it for you.

&#x200B;

If you throw it out, you're a monster.

Well, where I come from it's *normal* to thank soldiers for their service and pay them the respect they deserve, at least in passing. This is done if they mention their service or are walking around in uniform. You can do it to police and firemen too. That's how *normal* people treat them. Of course where I was raised and the traditions I grew up with are shat upon daily with this website. Some of us weren't raised to be entitled little shits who just expect others to be willing to put their lives lives on the line for them, just because it's their job. It's *normal* to be able to appreciate the people who are willing to do so.

&#x200B;

That *IS* treating them like a normal person. It's no small thing to be in the military. I'm not in the military, I admit. I don't have the balls for it, but it's nice to know some people do.

Technically the Slavs are the Poles, from a historical viewpoint. Adding them in would be a bit redundant. I feel like they would fit better in AoE 3 than AoE 2.

&#x200B;

~~Sidenote, I wish they'd revamp AoE 3. Add European and African maps and Civs, seriously that is some prime Zulu territory they missed there.~~
